  "preamble": "Raising of a near-open front vowel [æ] all the way to the close front [i]. The clear case is the Ikavian reflex of the Proto-Slavic yat *ě, a long open front vowel usually reconstructed as [æː], in South Chakavian dialects of Serbo-Croatian such as that of Vrgada: *věra 'faith' > vȉra and *dělo 'deed' > dȉlo. South Chakavian became Ikavian directly by the 13th century, while Štokavian Ikavian went through the diphthong /ie̯/.",
